 # Presentation Structure Guide
+
+## An Nhiên adaptation — apply before generic templates
+
+This is a UX design case study presented in Vietnamese, not a clinical experiment. Use: scenario → design questions → published evidence → project decisions → real UI → AI-assisted process → iteration evidence → limitations → planned user testing.
+
+Translate the original Hook/Context/Gap/Approach/Results/Implications/Closure as: bà Lan (explicitly a composite scenario), accessibility questions, verified papers, research-to-UI choices, actual Stitch artifacts, regressions and best-version choice, and next steps. “Results” means design artifacts and internal review, never health outcomes or real-user findings without data.
+
+Default to 16 main slides over 12–15 minutes; this is a project draft assumption, not a fixed upstream rule. Read `storyboard.md` for slide-level content. Include no more than 2–3 directly relevant verified papers in the main story. Keep other papers in an appendix after verification. Rehearse to check timing; do not mechanically enforce one slide per minute.
+
 
