 # Slide Design Principles for Scientific Presentations
+
+## An Nhiên adaptation — project visual direction takes priority
+
+Author in Canva MCP with editable text, charts and diagrams. Use 16:9; background #F6F7F2, primary #1F684B, text #202B25, secondary #D6EADF. Be Vietnam Pro, or Noto Sans if unavailable. Cover 48–60pt, slide title 32–40pt, body 22–28pt, labels 18–20pt, source footers 14–16pt. These are presentation choices, not Android app units. Keep 5% safe margins.
+
+One dominant composition per slide. Use actual UI screenshots at readable scale; before/after must use the same screen and viewport. Preserve image proportions and label versions. Avoid grids of decorative UI cards, medical stock imagery, and generated screenshots. Figures and UI artifacts must prove a point, not decorate a research claim.
+
+The original 6×6 rule is a heuristic, not a quota. Prefer 30–45 visible Vietnamese words per content slide when practical, with explanation in speaker notes. Choose the project palette over generic palettes below; do not infer psychological or medical effects from a color.
+
+Ignore implementation software suggestions below when creating this Canva deck. No Beamer/PPTX pipeline, external asset subscription, image model or API key is required by this adaptation.
+
 
