 # Evidence Hierarchy and Quality Assessment
+
+## An Nhiên adaptation — applicability before hierarchy
+
+For UI choices, assess the research question, actual participants, devices, tasks, methods, limitations and transfer to Vietnamese adults aged 65+. Do not treat a clinical RCT hierarchy as a universal ranking of UX evidence. A systematic review supports a direction only within the scope of its underlying studies.
+
+Every slide claim needs: source/DOI or repository path, supported claim, method/sample when relevant, limitation, applied UI decision and slide ID. Label VERIFIED / PARTIAL / LOCAL / PROPOSED. Research numbers must retain units; pt, px, dp and sp are not interchangeable.
+
+Six AI roleplays in `ux/persona.md` are simulations. Bà Lan/chị Mai are scenario characters. Stitch critic scores are internal rubric results, not SUS, usability percentages, user satisfaction or clinical benefit. New papers found now must not be narrated as sources used historically. Read `evidence-ledger.md` for verified project-specific sources.
+
 
